+# intel-online: branch coverage
+
+Every room-level and UI branch that `intel-online` added or changed, one row each: where it is, the branch in one line, and the test that fails when the branch is deleted. Each `tested` row was checked by deleting (or flipping) the branch on a scratch copy of the tree outside the repository, with its own `node_modules/@pirate-sea-race` links, and running the suites that reach it, in parallel batches: the server's, the protocol's and the web client's unit tests (`apps/server/src/intel.test.ts`, `packages/protocol/src/journal.test.ts` and `protocol.test.ts`, `apps/web/src/journal.test.ts` and `fruit.test.ts`); `tests/integration/intel.test.ts` and `intelSightings.test.ts`, and `ruins.test.ts`, `visibility.test.ts`, `reveals.test.ts` or `ledgerSeed.test.ts` where the branch reaches them; and the browser specs `tests/e2e/journal.spec.ts` (or `fruitDuel.spec.ts`) for what only the page does, one at a time. A baseline copy with no deletion passed every one of those suites first. The row names the tests that failed (the first two, and how many more), and the deletion id says what was deleted (`mutations.py` in the worker's scratch directory). None of those edits is committed.
